title: 'statement gossip: route v2 DHT propagation through the per-peer outbox'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, statements the orchestrator targets at a peer
    go through the same per-peer outbox as v1 propagation: one chunk in flight per peer, the
    shared in-flight byte budget, a bounded queue and a retry after a failed store fetch. The
    orchestrator's choice of peer is final, so the outbox applies no affinity filter of its
    own on that path. A queued statement that left the store or expired before its chunk went
    out, or was still queued when the peer disconnected, is counted in
    `undelivered_statements` under `missing_from_store` or `disconnected`.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
